feat(schema): reject bidi formatting code points in IRI parser

Exclude the RFC 3987 section 4.1 bidi formatting code points (LRM, RLM, LRE,
RLE, PDF, LRO, RLO) from the iunreserved predicate. Those code points fall inside
the ucschar range 0x00a0-0xd7ff, so IRI, AbsoluteIRI, IRIReference, and
RelativeIRIReference now reject inputs they previously accepted. Also updates the
RFC coverage notes and adds JSDoc to the exported IRI type aliases.
